{
  "delta_from_prior": "Acknowledged the Neon54/55 receipt (both peak 0 via global IALH congruences). Upgraded from the 24-var/80-clause disjoint-pair mediator fixture (neon_worstcase_auto_00092, which used disjoint 2-var pairs susceptible to Fable73 link-twin contraction and Fable86 PPC disjoint-gate pullback) to an 18-var/244-clause overlapping-XOR C7 x C7 vertex-cover/edge-transversal UNSAT fixture. Unlike Neon58 and neon_worstcase_auto_00092, the 14-var/63-clause compressed quotient has zero disjoint pairs, zero link-twins, and no nontrivial disjoint-gate factorization G^g, while also testing overlapping GF(2) basis forms (shared parity variables) in v5 compression.",
  "explanation": "1. AUDIT OF PINNED v5 (blq-composed-core-scc-emra-ialh5-v5)\nAuditing the supplied exact solver, compression.py, core_refutation.py, check_scc_and_growth.py, test_elim.py, and test_mra.py reveals no soundness bug:\n- compression.py: _verify_certificate rebuilds exact-support blocks from EVERY original clause in dense_formula(formula, ids), checks block_clause_counts partitions quotient, verifies local truth-table equality evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image) over every local assignment x in points(support) using only forms supported in that block, and verifies P*L = I over GF(2) entry-by-entry. Surjectivity of P plus blockwise conjunction yields exact equisatisfiability; no omitted-block bug exists.\n- core_refutation.py: probe() checks set(core).issubset(set(f)), requires compress_root(core) to succeed, and refutes ONLY when the compressed quotient is purely binary and two_sat(q) is False. SAT/UNKNOWN always falls back.\n- run_counting_core / refute / dependencies: up_survives() only performs forced unit propagation, so every table is a superset of projected models; verify_certificate() checks every local hull row and exact Fraction dual certificate independently of SymPy. canon_plus() (skew-symmetric signed SCC), elim_plus() (size-nonincreasing DP), and prune() (stronger-disjunct subsumption via below()) are sound.\n- Two non-bug operational observations from the code: (a) compress_root sorts candidate forms by (-block_frequency, popcount, bitmask), which deterministically dictates the ascending quotient branching order in run_counting_core(quotient, variables(quotient)); (b) step() memoizes on raw tuple(restrict(...)) before canon_plus(), so syntactically different pre-canonical states that reduce to the same canonical formula still repeat refute()/elim_plus() work.\n\n2. ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF NEON54/55 RECEIPT\nNeon54 and Neon55 (K6 near-parity witnesses) are retracted as growth witnesses: both actually peak 0 at the root because width-5 UP tables retain the XOR congruences after deleting an extra satisfying point, and the global integer lattice combines rows across windows without needing a union of whole blocks in one window.\n\n3. NEW 18-VARIABLE, 244-CLAUSE GROWTH FIXTURE (OVERLAPPING-XOR C7 x C7)\nConstructed as a direct counterexample to both v5 residual search and Fable's proposed nonlinear repairs (Fable73 link-twin contraction and Fable86 PPC prime-pullback collapse through disjoint gates):\n- Quotient Q (14 variables, 63 width-4 clauses):\n  * Left 7-cycle L on {1,7,3,9,5,11,13} with edges (1,7),(7,3),(3,9),(9,5),(5,11),(11,13),(13,1) and all 7 minimal vertex covers of C7 as negative width-4 clauses: (-7,-9,-11,-13), (-1,-3,-5,-13), (-1,-7,-9,-11), (-3,-5,-7,-13), (-1,-3,-9,-11), (-5,-7,-9,-13), (-1,-3,-5,-11).\n  * Right 7-cycle R on {2,8,4,10,6,12,14} (exact +1 variable shift) with its 7 edges and 7 minimal vertex covers.\n  * 49 positive width-4 cross-clauses (u, v, u', v') for every edge (u,v) of L and (u',v') of R.\n- Exact UNSAT proof: in C7, every independent set is contained in one of the 7 maximal independent sets of size 3 (rotations of {0,2,4}). Thus any assignment to L with no (0,0) edge has its 1-vertices containing one of the 7 minimal vertex covers, violating a negative clause. Hence every assignment satisfying L's negative clauses has a (0,0) edge in L, and symmetrically a (0,0) edge in R, contradicting the corresponding positive cross-clause (u, v, u', v').\n- Overlapping GF(2) lifting to 18 variables / 244 clauses (max width 6):\n  Replace q_7 = x_7 ^ x_17 and q_9 = x_9 ^ x_17 (shared parity variable x_17), q_11 = x_11 ^ x_15 and q_13 = x_13 ^ x_15 (shared x_15), and symmetrically on R with x_18 (for 8,10) and x_16 (for 12,14). Each clause expands by 2x per parity group hit (width +1 per group): 24 Left negative clauses, 24 Right negative clauses, and 49*4 = 196 width-6 cross-clauses (total 244 clauses, 63 blocks, local space 3904 <= 16384).\n\n4. PREDICTED BEHAVIOR ON PINNED v5\n- Root compression SUCCEEDS (not a skip): the 6 singletons x_1..x_6 (weight 1) and 8 overlapping XOR forms x_7^x_17, ..., x_14^x_16 (weight 2) each appear in 18 blocks, strictly exceeding every derived combination such as x_11^x_13 (8 blocks) or x_7^x_9 (3 blocks). Thus compress_root selects the exact 14-form compatible basis with q_1..q_6 = x_1..x_6 first, compresses 18 vars / 244 clauses to 14 vars / 63 clauses, and passes verify_certificate (and Lean check).\n- Core refutation returns UNKNOWN on both stages: every original block is already a complete coset of its stabilizer (|z| in {2,4}), and every quotient block has |z|=1, so core_refutation.probe removes 0 clauses ('no_clauses_removed') on both original and quotient.\n- Residual growth (predicted peak >= 9 on ascending quotient order 1..14):\n  * Root: no binary clauses (canon_plus idle), all clauses width 4 with full Z^w affine hulls on every window of size <= 5 (IALH-5 returns UNKNOWN with 0 constraints), and every variable has 4 negative / 14 positive occurrences (elim_plus stuck).\n  * Branching on 1, 2, 3, 4 (two non-adjacent vertices on L and two on R): on L, (1=0), (1=1,3=0), and (1=1,3=1) yield 3 distinct, pairwise incomparable STUCK residuals after elim_plus, none refuted by IALH-5. Symmetrically R yields 3 incomparable residuals, giving 3*3 = 9 simultaneous states at layer 4 (peak >= 9, exceeding the >= 4 threshold) while remaining compact enough (14 quotient vars, shrinking quickly after layer 4) to avoid timeout.\n\n5. CHALLENGE TO FABLE'S NONLINEAR PROPOSALS & REMAINING OBSTRUCTION\n- Unlike Neon58 and neon_worstcase_auto_00092, Q = C7 x C7 has NO disjoint 2-variable pairs, NO link-twins (every vertex has degree 2 in an odd cycle with a unique neighborhood), and NO nontrivial disjoint-gate prime-pullback factorization G^g. Both Fable73's link-twin contraction and Fable86's PPC collapse are completely inert on Q.\n- Scope note: this is a finite UNSAT growth fixture, not an asymptotic exponential lower bound (for general C_k x C_k, enumerating minimal vertex covers grows exponentially in k, so growth in k can still be polynomial in encoded input size). The remaining obstruction is finding a sound, polytime-checkable invariant that controls both frontier width and total preprocessing/certificate work on kernel-free, overlapping-constraint CNFs without fragile syntactic gate factorizations.",
